#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:1
msgid "Agent Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:3
msgid ""
"The Agent Panel is where you interact with AI agents that can read, write, "
"and run code in your project. Use it for code generation, refactoring, "
"debugging, documentation, and general questions."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:5
msgid ""
"Open it with `agent: new thread` from [the Command Palette](../getting-"
"started.md#command-palette) or click the ✨ icon in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:7
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:9
msgid ""
"If you're using the Agent Panel for the first time, you need to have at "
"least one LLM provider or external agent configured. You can do that by:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:12
msgid ""
"[subscribing to our Pro plan](https://zed.dev/pricing), so you have access "
"to our hosted models"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:13
msgid ""
"[using your own API keys](./llm-providers.md#use-your-own-keys), either from "
"model providers like Anthropic or model gateways like OpenRouter."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:14
msgid ""
"using an [external agent](./external-agents.md) like [Gemini CLI](./external-"
"agents.md#gemini-cli) or [Claude Code](./external-agents.md#claude-code)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:16
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:18
msgid ""
"With an LLM provider or external agent configured, type in the message "
"editor and press `enter` to submit. Expand the editor with <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">shift-alt-escape|shift-alt-escape</kbd> if you need "
"more room."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:20
msgid ""
"Responses stream in with indicators showing [which tools](./tools.md) the "
"model is using. The sections below cover what you can do from here."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:22
msgid ""
"Note that for external agents, like [Gemini CLI](./external-agents.md#gemini-"
"cli) or [Claude Code](./external-agents.md#claude-code), some of the "
"features outlined below may _not_ be supported—for example, _restoring "
"threads from history_, _checkpoints_, _token usage display_, and others. "
"Their availability varies depending on the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:24
msgid "Creating New Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:26
msgid "By default, the Agent Panel uses Zed's first-party agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:28
msgid ""
"To choose another agent, go to the plus button in the top-right of the Agent "
"Panel and pick either one of the [external agents](./external-agents.md) "
"installed out of the box or a new [Text Thread](./text-threads.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:30
msgid "Editing Messages"
msgstr "編輯訊息"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:32
msgid ""
"Any message that you send to the model is editable. You can click on the "
"card that contains your message and re-submit it with an adjusted prompt and/"
"or new pieces of context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:35
msgid "Queueing Messages"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:37
msgid ""
"Messages sent while the agent is in the generating state get, by default, "
"queued."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:39
msgid ""
"For the Zed agent, queued messages get sent at the next turn boundary, which "
"is usually between a tool call and a response, whereas for external agents, "
"the message gets sent at the end of the generation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:41
msgid ""
"You can edit or remove (an individual or all) queued messages. You can also "
"still interrupt the agent immediately if you want by either clicking on the "
"stop button or by clicking the \"Send Now\" (double-enter) on a queued "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:44
msgid "Checkpoints"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:46
msgid ""
"Every time the model performs an edit, you should see a \"Restore "
"Checkpoint\" button at the top of your message, allowing you to return your "
"code base to the state it was in prior to that message."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:48
msgid ""
"The checkpoint button appears even if you interrupt the thread midway "
"through an edit, as this is likely a moment when you've identified that the "
"agent is not heading in the right direction and you want to revert back."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:50
msgid "Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:52
msgid ""
"Right-click on any agent response in the thread view to access a context "
"menu with the following actions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:54
msgid ""
"**Copy Selection**: Copies the currently selected text as Markdown "
"(available when text is selected)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:55
msgid ""
"**Copy This Agent Response**: Copies the full text of the agent response you "
"right-clicked on."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:56
msgid ""
"**Scroll to Top / Scroll to Bottom**: Scrolls to the beginning or end of the "
"thread, depending on your current position."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:57
msgid ""
"**Open Thread as Markdown**: Opens the entire thread as a Markdown file in a "
"new tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:59
msgid "Navigating the Thread"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:61
msgid ""
"In long conversations, use the scroll button at the bottom of the panel to "
"jump to your most recent prompt."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:63
msgid "Navigating History"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:65
msgid ""
"To quickly navigate through recently updated threads, use the <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-j|ctrl-shift-j</kbd> binding when focused on "
"the panel's editor, or click the menu icon button at the top right of the "
"panel. Doing that will open a dropdown that shows you your six most recently "
"updated threads."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:68
msgid ""
"To view all historical conversations, reach for the `View All` option from "
"within the same menu or via the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-h|ctrl-"
"shift-h</kbd> binding."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:70
msgid ""
"Thread titles are auto-generated based on the conversation content. To "
"regenerate a title, open the ellipsis menu in the top right of the panel and "
"select \"Regenerate Thread Title\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:72
msgid "Following the Agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:74
msgid ""
"Follow the agent as it reads and edits files by clicking the crosshair icon "
"at the bottom left of the panel. Your editor will jump to each file the "
"agent touches."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:76
msgid ""
"You can also hold `cmd`/`ctrl` when submitting a message to automatically "
"follow."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:78
msgid "Get Notified"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:80
msgid ""
"If you send a prompt to the Agent and then put Zed in the background, you "
"can choose to be notified when its generation wraps up via:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:82
msgid "a visual notification that appears in the top right of your screen"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:83
msgid "a sound notification"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:85
msgid ""
"These notifications can be used together or individually, and you can use "
"the `agent.notify_when_agent_waiting` and `agent.play_sound_when_agent_done` "
"settings keys to customize that, including turning both off entirely."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:87
msgid "Reviewing Changes"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:89
msgid ""
"Once the agent has made changes to your project, the panel will surface "
"which files, how many of them, and how many lines have been edited."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:91
msgid ""
"To see which files specifically have been edited, expand the accordion bar "
"that shows up right above the message editor or click the `Review Changes` "
"button (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-ctrl-r|ctrl-shift-r</kbd>), which "
"opens a special multi-buffer tab with all changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:93
msgid ""
"You can accept or reject each individual change hunk, or the whole set of "
"changes made by the agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:95
msgid ""
"Edit diffs also appear in singleton buffers. If your active tab had edits "
"made by the AI, you'll see diffs with the same accept/reject controls as in "
"the multi-buffer. You can turn this off, though, through the `agent."
"single_file_review` setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:99
msgid "Adding Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:101
msgid ""
"The agent can search your codebase to find relevant context, but providing "
"it explicitly improves response quality and reduces latency."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:103
msgid ""
"Add context by typing `@` in the message editor. You can mention files, "
"directories, symbols, previous threads, rules files, and diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:105
msgid ""
"Copying images and pasting them in the panel's message editor is also "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:107
msgid ""
"When you paste multi-line code selections copied from a buffer, Zed "
"automatically formats them as @-mentions with the file context. To paste "
"content without this automatic formatting, use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-"
"shift-v|ctrl-shift-v</kbd> to paste raw text directly."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:110
msgid "Selection as Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:112
msgid ""
"Additionally, you can also select text in a buffer and add it as context by "
"using the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd->|ctrl-></kbd> keybinding, running "
"the <code class=\"hljs\">agent: add selection to thread</code> action, or "
"choosing the \"Selection\" item in the `@` menu."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:114
msgid "Token Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:116
msgid ""
"Zed surfaces how many tokens you are consuming for your currently active "
"thread near the profile selector in the panel's message editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:118
msgid ""
"Once you approach the model's context window, a banner appears above the "
"message editor suggesting to start a new thread with the current one "
"summarized and added as context. You can also do this at any time with an "
"ongoing thread via the \"Agent Options\" menu on the top right, where you'll "
"see a \"New from Summary\" button, as well as simply @-mentioning a past "
"thread in a new one.."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:121
msgid "Changing Models"
msgstr "變更模型"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:123
msgid ""
"After you've configured your LLM providers—either via [a custom API key](./"
"llm-providers.md) or through [Zed's hosted models](./models.md)—you can "
"switch between their models by clicking on the model selector on the message "
"editor or by using the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-/|ctrl-alt-/</kbd> "
"keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:125
msgid ""
"The same model can be offered via multiple providers - for example, Claude "
"Sonnet 4 is available via Zed Pro, OpenRouter, Anthropic directly, and more. "
"Make sure you've selected the correct model **_provider_** for the model "
"you'd like to use, delineated by the logo to the left of the model in the "
"model selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:128
msgid "Favoriting Models"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:130
msgid ""
"You can mark specific models as favorites either through the model selector, "
"by clicking on the star icon button that appears as you hover the model, or "
"through your settings via the `agent.favorite_models` settings key."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:132
msgid ""
"Cycle through your favorites with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-tab|alt-l</"
"kbd> without opening the model selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:134
msgid "Using Tools"
msgstr "使用工具"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:136
msgid ""
"The Agent Panel supports tool calling, which enables agentic editing. Zed "
"includes [built-in tools](./tools.md) for searching your codebase, editing "
"files, running terminal commands, and fetching web content."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:139
msgid ""
"You can also extend the set of available tools via [MCP Servers](./mcp.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:141
msgid "Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:143
msgid ""
"Profiles act as a way to group tools. Zed offers three built-in profiles and "
"you can create as many custom ones as you want."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:146
msgid "Built-in Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:148
msgid ""
"`Write`: A profile with tools to allow the LLM to write to your files and "
"run terminal commands. This one essentially has all built-in tools turned on."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:149
msgid ""
"`Ask`: A profile with read-only tools. Best for asking questions about your "
"code base without the concern of the agent making changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:150
msgid ""
"`Minimal`: A profile with no tools. Best for general conversations with the "
"LLM where no knowledge of your code base is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:152
msgid ""
"You can explore the exact tools enabled in each profile by clicking on the "
"profile selector button > `Configure` button > the one you want to check out."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:154
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can also use either the command palette, by running <code "
"class=\"hljs\">agent: manage profiles</code>, or the keybinding directly, "
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-p|ctrl-alt-p</kbd>, to have access to the "
"profile management modal."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:156
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-tab|shift-tab</kbd> to switch between "
"profiles without opening the modal."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:158
msgid "Custom Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:160
msgid ""
"You can also create a custom profile through the Agent Profile modal. From "
"there, you can choose to `Add New Profile` or fork an existing one with a "
"custom name and your preferred set of tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:163
msgid ""
"It's also possible to override built-in profiles. In the Agent Profile "
"modal, select a built-in profile, navigate to `Configure Tools`, and "
"rearrange the tools you'd like to keep or remove."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:166
msgid ""
"Zed will store this profile in your settings using the same profile name as "
"the default you overrode."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:168
msgid ""
"All custom profiles can be edited via the UI or by hand under the `agent."
"profiles` key in your `settings.json` file."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:170
msgid ""
"To delete a custom profile, open the Agent Profile modal, select the profile "
"you want to remove, and click the delete button."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:172
msgid "Tool Approval"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:174
msgid ""
"Zed's Agent Panel surfaces the `agent.always_allow_tool_actions` setting "
"that, if turned to `false`, will require you to give permission to any "
"editing attempt as well as tool calls coming from MCP servers."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:176
msgid ""
"You can change that by setting this key to `true` in either your `settings."
"json` or via the Agent Panel's settings view."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:178
msgid ""
"You can also give more granular permissions through the dropdown that "
"appears in the UI whenever the agent requests authorization to run a tool "
"call."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:180
msgid "Model Support"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:182
msgid ""
"Tool calling needs to be individually supported by each model and model "
"provider. Therefore, despite the presence of tools, some models may not have "
"the ability to pick them up yet in Zed. You should see a \"No tools\" label "
"if you select a model that falls into this case."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:186
msgid ""
"All [Zed's hosted models](./models.md) support tool calling out-of-the-box."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:188
msgid "MCP Servers"
msgstr "MCP 伺服器"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:190
msgid ""
"Similarly to the built-in tools, some models may not support all tools "
"included in a given MCP Server. Zed's UI will inform you about this via a "
"warning icon that appears close to the model selector."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:193
msgid "Text Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:195
msgid ""
"[\"Text Threads\"](./text-threads.md) present your conversation with the LLM "
"in a different format—as raw text. With text threads, you have full control "
"over the conversation data. You can remove and edit responses from the LLM, "
"swap roles, and include more context earlier in the conversation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:199
msgid ""
"Text threads are Zed's original assistant panel format, preserved for users "
"who want direct control over conversation data. Autonomous code editing "
"(where the agent writes to files) is only available in the default thread "
"format, not text threads."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:202
msgid "Errors and Debugging"
msgstr "錯誤與除錯"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:204
msgid ""
"In case of any error or strange LLM response behavior, the best way to help "
"the Zed team debug is by reaching for the `agent: open thread as markdown` "
"action and attaching that data as part of your issue on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:206
msgid ""
"You can also open threads as Markdown by clicking on the file icon button, "
"to the right of the thumbs down button, when focused on the panel's editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:208
msgid "Feedback"
msgstr "意見反饋"

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:210
msgid ""
"You can rate agent responses to help improve Zed's system prompt and tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:212
msgid ""
"Note that rating responses will send your data related to that response to "
"Zed's servers. See [AI Improvement](./ai-improvement.md) and [Privacy and "
"Security](./privacy-and-security.md) for more information about Zed's "
"approach to AI improvement, privacy, and security. **_If you don't want data "
"persisted on Zed's servers, don't rate_**. We will not collect data for "
"improving our Agentic offering without you explicitly rating responses."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:216
msgid ""
"The best way you can help influence the next change to Zed's system prompt "
"and tools is by rating the LLM's response via the thumbs up/down buttons at "
"the end of every response. In case of a thumbs down, a new text area will "
"show up where you can add more specifics about what happened."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/agent-panel.md:218
msgid ""
"You can provide feedback on the thread at any point after the agent "
"responds, and multiple times within the same thread."
msgstr ""
